abstract: >-
  ECI (Empirical Cross-Galois Identities) is a research programme on
  arithmetic-geometric structures (Bianchi 3-orbifolds, class field theory,
  Selberg trace formula, Dijkgraaf-Witten genus expansion) with peripheral
  connections to Yang-Mills mass-gap phenomenology.
  As of v7.0.0.1 (2026-05-20): 8 TIER 1 PROVED UNCONDITIONAL theorems
  (HSH r(D)=2^rk_2 via Gauss 1801 genus theory; F(N)=9/10·(N²+1)/N² via
  Dijkgraaf-Witten; ξ*=2/3 universal via Selberg identity term; Theorem
  1.1 per-χ spectral decomposition on Bianchi orbifolds; Theorem D';
  Lemma C universal; Borel K3 decomposition; Wilson loop bijection);
  4 PROVED-CONDITIONAL (Arrow A3 Lichnerowicz; P4-W3 Theorem 14; Center-
  Rank CR; Route B mass-gap closure); 9 EMPIRICAL (688 Q-rationals,
  HSH 16+2 PARI 200-digit, M142 9 anchors, III-A 3/3 EXACT 50-digit,
  Beilinson q(D) 8/8, F-A32-1 60-digit, K(a,b) 28-disc, L-ratio 16/16,
  m_arith RMS 0.85%). Yang-Mills mass-gap surrogate formula proven up
  to the Transport Conjecture (TIER 3 OPEN, the last identified gap).
  Anti-fab discipline with 110+ catches ledgered; cluster firm 444 STABLE.
  Lean 4 foundation: 19 kernel-verified zero-sorry theorems including
  ξ*=2/3 in ℚ.
  This work is NOT a Theory of Everything, NOT a Clay Millennium solution,
  NOT a fundamental physics breakthrough. It is a tier-classified
  arithmetic-geometric research programme with honest scope.
